{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/watermelon-around-the-world/audio/main-20a19b70b446.mp3","durationSec":201.744,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.82,"text":"Watermelon's story began in Africa."},{"start":2.38,"end":8.8,"text":"A pale melon from Sudan called the Kordofan melon is the closest known relative of today's watermelon."},{"start":9.46,"end":10.92,"text":"It may be one of its ancestors."},{"start":10.92,"end":18.46,"text":"Pictures in ancient Egyptian tombs suggest that people ate a watermelon-like fruit more than 4,000 years ago."},{"start":19.2,"end":22.7,"text":"Those early fruits were not always bright red or very sweet."},{"start":22.7,"end":26.42,"text":"Farmers saved seeds from fruit with qualities they liked."},{"start":27.14,"end":31.72,"text":"Over many generations, watermelon became sweeter, and red flesh became common."},{"start":32.34,"end":34.32,"text":"This change took a very long time."},{"start":35.88,"end":39.84,"text":"In China, people do not only enjoy the red flesh."},{"start":40.82,"end":43.38,"text":"Roasted watermelon seeds are also a popular snack."},{"start":44.06,"end":47.74,"text":"Some farmers grow special seeded watermelons mainly for their seeds."},{"start":48.56,"end":51.94,"text":"After the fruit is ready, the seeds are collected and roasted."},{"start":52.8,"end":55.8,"text":"People open the hard shell and eat the small part inside."},{"start":55.8,"end":60.44,"text":"This takes time, so the snack can be enjoyed slowly while people talk or rest."},{"start":61.44,"end":67.52,"text":"One plant can therefore give people two very different foods: juicy fruit and dry, crunchy seeds."},{"start":68.4,"end":72.1,"text":"Some people in Turkiye eat cold watermelon with white cheese in summer."},{"start":72.62,"end":75.66,"text":"The fruit is sweet and juicy, but the cheese is salty."},{"start":76.42,"end":78.66,"text":"The two different tastes can work well together."},{"start":79.8,"end":82.04,"text":"Size can also give watermelon a special meaning."},{"start":82.04,"end":88.3,"text":"Diyarbakir holds a culture and watermelon festival with a competition for very large local fruit."},{"start":89.06,"end":93.4,"text":"Watermelons in this competition can weigh between 15 and 70 kilograms."},{"start":94.6,"end":97.42,"text":"The event celebrates local farming and pride."},{"start":98.14,"end":102.36,"text":"This example connects a simple summer meal with a long farming tradition."},{"start":103.5,"end":109.16,"text":"In Mexico, watermelon can become a cold drink called agua fresca."},{"start":109.16,"end":111.98,"text":"Aguas frescas are an important part of Mexican food culture."},{"start":112.42,"end":117.62,"text":"People make different kinds with fruit or seeds, water, ice, and sometimes sugar."},{"start":118.4,"end":122.38,"text":"For a watermelon version, the fruit is mixed with water and served cold."},{"start":123.34,"end":126.06,"text":"Recipes can change from one family or shop to another."},{"start":126.8,"end":130.24,"text":"This drink is easy to share from a large container on a hot day."},{"start":130.94,"end":134.44,"text":"Here, people enjoy the fresh taste without eating a slice."},{"start":135.46,"end":138.7,"text":"Most people eat the soft flesh and throw away the rind."},{"start":139.28,"end":144.62,"text":"In parts of the southern United States, however, people make pickles from the pale part of the rind."},{"start":145.34,"end":148.46,"text":"They first remove the fruit and the hard dark-green skin."},{"start":149.1,"end":152.32,"text":"The crisp pale rind can then be prepared as a pickle."},{"start":153.14,"end":157.16,"text":"Home cooks and small producers have kept this food tradition alive."},{"start":157.74,"end":161.78,"text":"It turns a part that often becomes waste into something people can eat."},{"start":162.36,"end":165.48,"text":"The watermelon is not only a sweet dessert anymore."},{"start":165.92,"end":171.18,"text":"In Zentsuji City in Kagawa, Japan, some farmers grow cube-shaped watermelons."},{"start":171.7,"end":174.88,"text":"They place the young fruit inside special containers as it grows."},{"start":175.94,"end":179.22,"text":"Local farmers have developed this skill since the late 1960s."},{"start":179.7,"end":185.2,"text":"The regular shape and beautiful stripes make these watermelons unusual, and they can sell for high prices."},{"start":186.1,"end":189.04,"text":"People may value them as local gifts or display pieces."},{"start":190.08,"end":192.58,"text":"Their shape does not mean that they taste better."},{"start":193.26,"end":200.94,"text":"Like roasted seeds, cheese, drinks, and pickles, the square fruit shows that people can give the same plant very different meanings."}],"words":[{"text":"Watermelon's","start":0,"end":0.7},{"text":"story","start":0.7,"end":0.9},{"text":"began","start":0.9,"end":1.24},{"text":"in","start":1.24,"end":1.42},{"text":"Africa","start":1.42,"end":1.82},{"text":"A","start":2.38,"end":2.42},{"text":"pale","start":2.42,"end":2.74},{"text":"melon","start":2.74,"end":3.12},{"text":"from","start":3.12,"end":3.34},{"text":"Sudan","start":3.34,"end":3.78},{"text":"called","start":3.78,"end":4.18},{"text":"the","start":4.18,"end":4.44},{"text":"Kordofan","start":4.44,"end":5.1},{"text":"melon","start":5.1,"end":5.54},{"text":"is","start":5.54,"end":5.98},{"text":"the","start":5.98,"end":6.16},{"text":"closest","start":6.16,"end":6.58},{"text":"known","start":6.58,"end":6.94},{"text":"relative","start":6.94,"end":7.46},{"text":"of","start":7.46,"end":7.78},{"text":"today's","start":7.78,"end":8.24},{"text":"watermelon","start":8.24,"end":8.8},{"text":"It","start":9.46,"end":9.58},{"text":"may","start":9.58,"end":9.76},{"text":"be","start":9.76,"end":9.9},{"text":"one","start":9.9,"end":10.04},{"text":"of","start":10.04,"end":10.16},{"text":"its","start":10.16,"end":10.28},{"text":"ancestors","start":10.28,"end":10.92},{"text":"Pictures","start":10.92,"e